-- coa15-ch2.l4: Part 18, Chapter 2 (Financial assistance for purchase of own shares), ss 677 to 683
-- (lines 8931-9029 of ukpga-2006-46.txt). Layer 1: the law, objectively, with no seat.
--
-- SOURCE. A plain-text rendering of the Act from legislation.gov.uk made by a converter script; it is not the
-- official text and nothing here is "verified against the official text". Quote lines are checked by srcrefs.py.
--
-- HOW TO READ AN ANSWER: as in coa15-ch1.l4. JUST FALSE where the text says no in its own words (a "means" definition, a
-- condition introduced by "if", "where", "when", "unless", a flat negative); NOTHING where it lists without closing the list,
-- says "includes", is silent, points outside the sources or limits a grant or prohibition by a scope it names.

-- ---- s 677: meaning of "financial assistance" ------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 677(1) form of assistance` IS ONE OF
    `s 677(1)(a) a gift`
    `s 677(1)(b)(i) a guarantee, security or indemnity`
    `s 677(1)(b)(i) an indemnity in respect of the indemnifier's own neglect or default`
    `s 677(1)(b)(ii) a release or waiver`
    `s 677(1)(c)(i) a loan, or another agreement under which any of the obligations of the person giving the assistance are to be fulfilled at a time when any obligation of another party remains unfulfilled`
    `s 677(1)(c)(ii) a novation of, or an assignment of rights arising under, a loan or such other agreement`
    `s 677(1)(d) any other financial assistance`

-- src:8934 | (1) In this Chapter “financial assistance” means—
-- src:8935 | (a) financial assistance given by way of gift,
-- src:8936 | (b) financial assistance given—
-- src:8937 | (i) by way of guarantee, security or indemnity (other than an indemnity in respect of the indemnifier's own neglect or default), or
-- src:8938 | (ii) by way of release or waiver,
-- src:8939 | (c) financial assistance given—
-- src:8940 | (i) by way of a loan or any other agreement under which any of the obligations of the person giving the assistance are to be fulfilled at a time when in accordance with the agreement any obligation of another party to the agreement remains unfulfilled, or
-- src:8941 | (ii) by way of the novation of, or the assignment (in Scotland, assignation) of rights arising under, a loan or such other agreement, or
-- src:8942 | (d) any other financial assistance given by a company where—
-- src:8943 | (i) the net assets of the company are reduced to a material extent by the giving of the assistance, or
-- src:8944 | (ii) the company has no net assets.
@ref s 677(1) Meaning of "financial assistance" (src:8934-8944)
GIVEN form IS A `s 677(1) form of assistance`
      `the net assets of the company are reduced to a material extent by the giving of the assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the net assets of the company, as section 677(2) works them out` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 677(1) the assistance given by the company is financial assistance` MEANS
    CONSIDER form
    WHEN `s 677(1)(a) a gift` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 677(1)(b)(i) a guarantee, security or indemnity` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 677(1)(b)(ii) a release or waiver` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 677(1)(c)(i) a loan, or another agreement under which any of the obligations of the person giving the assistance are to be fulfilled at a time when any obligation of another party remains unfulfilled` THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN `s 677(1)(c)(ii) a novation of, or an assignment of rights arising under, a loan or such other agreement` THEN JUST TRUE
    -- "(other than an indemnity in respect of the indemnifier's own neglect or default)": that indemnity is not within (b)(i); paragraph (d) may still catch it
    WHEN `s 677(1)(b)(i) an indemnity in respect of the indemnifier's own neglect or default` THEN
         IF `the net assets of the company are reduced to a material extent by the giving of the assistance` OR `the net assets of the company, as section 677(2) works them out` AT MOST 0
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "“financial assistance” means— ... (b) financial assistance given— (i) by way of guarantee, security or indemnity (other than an indemnity in respect of the indemnifier's own neglect or default)"
    WHEN `s 677(1)(d) any other financial assistance` THEN
         IF `the net assets of the company are reduced to a material extent by the giving of the assistance` OR `the net assets of the company, as section 677(2) works them out` AT MOST 0
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(d) any other financial assistance given by a company where (i) the net assets of the company are reduced to a material extent by the giving of the assistance, or (ii) the company has no net assets"

-- src:8945 | (2) “Net assets” here means the aggregate amount of the company's assets less the aggregate amount of its liabilities.
@ref s 677(2) "Net assets" means the aggregate amount of the company's assets less the aggregate amount of its liabilities (src:8945-8945)
GIVEN `the aggregate amount of the company's assets` IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate amount of its liabilities, as section 677(3) works them out` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 677(2) the net assets of the company` MEANS
    `the aggregate amount of the company's assets` MINUS `the aggregate amount of its liabilities, as section 677(3) works them out`

-- src:8946 | (3) For this purpose a company's liabilities include—
-- src:8947 | (a) where the company draws up Companies Act individual accounts, any provision of a kind specified for the purposes of this subsection by regulations under section 396, and
-- src:8948 | (b) where the company draws up IAS individual accounts, any provision made in those accounts.
@ref s 677(3) A company's liabilities include provisions of the kind specified by regulations under section 396 and, for IAS accounts, any provision made (src:8946-8948)
GIVEN `the aggregate amount of the company's liabilities apart from any provision` IS A NUMBER
      `the company draws up Companies Act individual accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provisions of a kind specified for the purposes of subsection (3) by regulations under section 396` IS A NUMBER
      `the company draws up IAS individual accounts` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provisions made in those IAS accounts` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 677(3) the aggregate amount of the company's liabilities` MEANS
    `the aggregate amount of the company's liabilities apart from any provision`
      PLUS (IF `the company draws up Companies Act individual accounts` THEN `the provisions of a kind specified for the purposes of subsection (3) by regulations under section 396` ELSE 0)
      PLUS (IF `the company draws up IAS individual accounts` THEN `the provisions made in those IAS accounts` ELSE 0)

-- ---- ss 678 and 679: the prohibition ---------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 678(1) who gives the assistance` IS ONE OF
    `s 678(1) the company whose shares are acquired`
    `s 678(1) a company that is a subsidiary of that company`
    `s 678(1) another company`

DECLARE `s 678(1) act of the company` IS ONE OF
    `s 678(1) give financial assistance directly or indirectly for the purpose of an acquisition of shares`
    `s 678(3) give financial assistance directly or indirectly for the purpose of reducing or discharging a liability incurred for an acquisition of shares`
    `s 679(1) give financial assistance directly or indirectly for the purpose of an acquisition of shares in its private holding company`
    `s 679(3) give financial assistance directly or indirectly for the purpose of reducing or discharging a liability incurred for an acquisition of shares in its private holding company`

-- src:8951 | (1) Where a person is acquiring or proposing to acquire shares in a public company, it is not lawful for that company, or a company that is a subsidiary of that company, to give financial assistance directly or indirectly for the purpose of the acquisition before or at the same time as the acquisition takes place.
@ref s 678(1) Assistance for acquisition of shares in a public company (src:8951-8951)
GIVEN `a person is acquiring or proposing to acquire shares in a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      giver IS A `s 678(1) who gives the assistance`
      `the assistance is financial assistance` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the assistance is given directly or indirectly for the purpose of the acquisition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assistance is given before or at the same time as the acquisition takes place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 678(1) it is not lawful for the company to give the financial assistance` MEANS
    IF (NOT `a person is acquiring or proposing to acquire shares in a public company`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person is acquiring or proposing to acquire shares in a public company"
    ELSE CONSIDER giver
         WHEN `s 678(1) another company` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for that company, or a company that is a subsidiary of that company, to give financial assistance"
         OTHERWISE
              IF (NOT `the assistance is given directly or indirectly for the purpose of the acquisition`) OR (NOT `the assistance is given before or at the same time as the acquisition takes place`)
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "financial assistance directly or indirectly for the purpose of the acquisition before or at the same time as the acquisition takes place"
              ELSE `the assistance is financial assistance`

@ref s 678(1) Assistance for acquisition of shares in a public company (src:8951-8951)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 678(1) act of the company`
`s 678(1) the company shant give the financial assistance` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    SHANT `s 678(1) give financial assistance directly or indirectly for the purpose of an acquisition of shares`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 678(1): financial assistance was given for the purpose of an acquisition of shares in a public company"

-- src:8952 | (2) Subsection (1) does not prohibit a company from giving financial assistance for the acquisition of shares in it or its holding company if—
-- src:8953 | (a) the company's principal purpose in giving the assistance is not to give it for the purpose of any such acquisition, or
-- src:8954 | (b) the giving of the assistance for that purpose is only an incidental part of some larger purpose of the company,
-- src:8955 | and the assistance is given in good faith in the interests of the company.
@ref s 678(2) Subsection (1) does not prohibit assistance whose principal purpose is not the acquisition, given in good faith (src:8952-8955)
GIVEN `the company's principal purpose in giving the assistance is not to give it for the purpose of any such acquisition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the giving of the assistance for that purpose is only an incidental part of some larger purpose of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assistance is given in good faith in the interests of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 678(2) subsection (1) does not prohibit the assistance` MEANS
    IF (`the company's principal purpose in giving the assistance is not to give it for the purpose of any such acquisition`
        OR `the giving of the assistance for that purpose is only an incidental part of some larger purpose of the company`)
       AND `the assistance is given in good faith in the interests of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not prohibit a company from giving financial assistance ... if (a) ... or (b) ..., and the assistance is given in good faith in the interests of the company"

-- src:8956 | (3) Where—
-- src:8957 | (a) a person has acquired shares in a company, and
-- src:8958 | (b) a liability has been incurred (by that or another person) for the purpose of the acquisition,
-- src:8959 | it is not lawful for that company, or a company that is a subsidiary of that company, to give financial assistance directly or indirectly for the purpose of reducing or discharging the liability if, at the time the assistance is given, the company in which the shares were acquired is a public company.
@ref s 678(3) Assistance for reducing or discharging a liability incurred for an acquisition, where the company is a public company (src:8956-8959)
GIVEN `a person has acquired shares in a company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a liability has been incurred (by that or another person) for the purpose of the acquisition` IS A BOOLEAN
      giver IS A `s 678(1) who gives the assistance`
      `the assistance is financial assistance` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the assistance is given directly or indirectly for the purpose of reducing or discharging the liability` IS A BOOLEAN
      `at the time the assistance is given the company in which the shares were acquired is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 678(3) it is not lawful for the company to give the financial assistance to reduce or discharge the liability` MEANS
    IF (NOT `a person has acquired shares in a company`) OR (NOT `a liability has been incurred (by that or another person) for the purpose of the acquisition`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where— (a) a person has acquired shares in a company, and (b) a liability has been incurred (by that or another person) for the purpose of the acquisition"
    ELSE CONSIDER giver
         WHEN `s 678(1) another company` THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "for that company, or a company that is a subsidiary of that company, to give financial assistance"
         OTHERWISE
              IF (NOT `the assistance is given directly or indirectly for the purpose of reducing or discharging the liability`) OR (NOT `at the time the assistance is given the company in which the shares were acquired is a public company`)
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for the purpose of reducing or discharging the liability if, at the time the assistance is given, the company in which the shares were acquired is a public company"
              ELSE `the assistance is financial assistance`

@ref s 678(3) Assistance for reducing or discharging a liability incurred for an acquisition, where the company is a public company (src:8956-8959)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 678(1) act of the company`
`s 678(3) the company shant give the financial assistance to reduce or discharge the liability` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    SHANT `s 678(3) give financial assistance directly or indirectly for the purpose of reducing or discharging a liability incurred for an acquisition of shares`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 678(3): financial assistance was given to reduce or discharge a liability incurred for an acquisition of shares in a public company"

-- src:8960 | (4) Subsection (3) does not prohibit a company from giving financial assistance if—
-- src:8961 | (a) the company's principal purpose in giving the assistance is not to reduce or discharge any liability incurred by a person for the purpose of the acquisition of shares in the company or its holding company, or
-- src:8962 | (b) the reduction or discharge of any such liability is only an incidental part of some larger purpose of the company,
-- src:8963 | and the assistance is given in good faith in the interests of the company.
@ref s 678(4) Subsection (3) does not prohibit assistance whose principal purpose is not to reduce or discharge the liability, given in good faith (src:8960-8963)
GIVEN `the company's principal purpose in giving the assistance is not to reduce or discharge any liability incurred by a person for the purpose of the acquisition of shares in the company or its holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the reduction or discharge of any such liability is only an incidental part of some larger purpose of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assistance is given in good faith in the interests of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 678(4) subsection (3) does not prohibit the assistance` MEANS
    IF (`the company's principal purpose in giving the assistance is not to reduce or discharge any liability incurred by a person for the purpose of the acquisition of shares in the company or its holding company`
        OR `the reduction or discharge of any such liability is only an incidental part of some larger purpose of the company`)
       AND `the assistance is given in good faith in the interests of the company`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "does not prohibit a company from giving financial assistance if (a) ... or (b) ..., and the assistance is given in good faith in the interests of the company"

-- s 678(5) and s 679(5): "This section has effect subject to sections 681 and 682". The prohibition of the subsections above gives way to an exception that holds.
-- src:8964 | (5) This section has effect subject to sections 681 and 682 (unconditional and conditional exceptions to prohibition).
@ref s 678(5) This section has effect subject to sections 681 and 682 (src:8964-8964)
GIVEN prohibition IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `subsection (2) or (4) does not prohibit the assistance` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 681(1) neither section 678 nor section 679 prohibits the transaction` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 682(1) neither section 678 nor section 679 prohibits the transaction` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 678(5) the assistance is prohibited by section 678 as it has effect subject to sections 681 and 682` MEANS
    IF (`subsection (2) or (4) does not prohibit the assistance` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
       OR (`s 681(1) neither section 678 nor section 679 prohibits the transaction` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
       OR (`s 682(1) neither section 678 nor section 679 prohibits the transaction` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Subsection (1) does not prohibit"; "Neither section 678 nor section 679 prohibits a transaction to which this section applies"
    ELSE prohibition

-- src:8966 | (1) Where a person is acquiring or proposing to acquire shares in a private company, it is not lawful for a public company that is a subsidiary of that company to give financial assistance directly or indirectly for the purpose of the acquisition before or at the same time as the acquisition takes place.
@ref s 679(1) Assistance by a public company for acquisition of shares in its private holding company (src:8966-8966)
GIVEN `a person is acquiring or proposing to acquire shares in a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the giver is a public company that is a subsidiary of that company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assistance is financial assistance` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the assistance is given directly or indirectly for the purpose of the acquisition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assistance is given before or at the same time as the acquisition takes place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 679(1) it is not lawful for the public company to give the financial assistance` MEANS
    IF (NOT `a person is acquiring or proposing to acquire shares in a private company`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Where a person is acquiring or proposing to acquire shares in a private company"
    ELSE IF (NOT `the giver is a public company that is a subsidiary of that company`)
         THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "it is not lawful for a public company that is a subsidiary of that company to give financial assistance"
         ELSE IF (NOT `the assistance is given directly or indirectly for the purpose of the acquisition`) OR (NOT `the assistance is given before or at the same time as the acquisition takes place`)
              THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "financial assistance directly or indirectly for the purpose of the acquisition before or at the same time as the acquisition takes place"
              ELSE `the assistance is financial assistance`

@ref s 679(1) Assistance by a public company for acquisition of shares in its private holding company (src:8966-8966)
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `s 678(1) act of the company`
`s 679(1) the public company shant give the financial assistance` MEANS
    PARTY Company
    SHANT `s 679(1) give financial assistance directly or indirectly for the purpose of an acquisition of shares in its private holding company`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY Company BECAUSE "s 679(1): a public company gave financial assistance for the purpose of an acquisition of shares in its private holding company"

