-- ---- s 680: prohibited financial assistance an offence --------------------------------------------------

-- src:8981 | (1) If a company contravenes section 678(1) or (3) or section 679(1) or (3) (prohibited financial assistance) an offence is committed by—
-- src:8982 | (a) the company, and
-- src:8983 | (b) every officer of the company who is in default.
@ref s 680(1) Offence (src:8981-8983)
GIVEN `the company contravenes section 678(1) or (3) or section 679(1) or (3)` IS A BOOLEAN
      person IS A `s 658(2) person charged`
      `s 1121 the officer is in default` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 680(1) the person commits an offence` MEANS
    -- fork F-not-in-default: an officer who is not in default is answered NOTHING (the text charges only officers in default); the other reading answers JUST FALSE
    IF (NOT `the company contravenes section 678(1) or (3) or section 679(1) or (3)`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "If a company contravenes section 678(1) or (3) or section 679(1) or (3) (prohibited financial assistance)"
    ELSE CONSIDER person
         WHEN `s 658(2) the company` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `s 658(2) an officer of the company` THEN
              CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who is in default"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is in default is s 1121 (coa24)
         WHEN `s 658(2) a director of the company` THEN
              CONSIDER `s 1121 the officer is in default`
              WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
              WHEN JUST FALSE THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): "who is in default"
              WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the person is in default is s 1121 (coa24)
         OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (limited by its own wording): the text charges the company and every officer of the company who is in default

-- src:8984 | (2) A person guilty of an offence under this section is liable—
-- src:8985 | (a) on conviction on indictment, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding two years or a fine (or both);
-- src:8986 | (b) on summary conviction—
-- src:8987 | (i) in England and Wales, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding twelve months or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both);
-- src:8988 | (ii) in Scotland or Northern Ireland, to imprisonment for a term not exceeding six months, or to a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum (or both).
@ref s 680(2) Penalty (src:8984-8988)
GIVEN how IS A `Mode of conviction`
GIVETH A MAYBE Penalty
`s 680(2) the penalty on conviction` MEANS
    -- Penalty OF  how convicted,  imprisonment not exceeding,  fine not exceeding,  daily default fine,  imprisonment and fine together
    CONSIDER how
    WHEN `on conviction on indictment` THEN
         JUST (Penalty OF `on conviction on indictment`, JUST (Period OF 2, Years), JUST `a fine without a stated limit`, NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in England and Wales` THEN
         JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in England and Wales`, JUST (Period OF 12, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Scotland` THEN
         JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Scotland`, JUST (Period OF 6, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE)
    WHEN `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland` THEN
         JUST (Penalty OF `on summary conviction in Northern Ireland`, JUST (Period OF 6, Months), JUST (`a fine not exceeding the statutory maximum` 1), NOTHING, TRUE)
    OTHERWISE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (silent): the text gives the penalty on indictment and on summary conviction by place; a summary conviction with no place named is not a case it states

-- ---- s 681: unconditional exceptions ----------------------------------------------------------------------

DECLARE `s 681(2) transaction` IS ONE OF
    `s 681(2)(a)(i) a distribution of the company's assets by way of dividend lawfully made`
    `s 681(2)(a)(ii) a distribution of the company's assets in the course of a company's winding up`
    `s 681(2)(b) an allotment of bonus shares`
    `s 681(2)(c) a reduction of capital under Chapter 10 of Part 17`
    `s 681(2)(d) a redemption of shares under Chapter 3 of this Part`
    `s 681(2)(d) a purchase of shares under Chapter 4 of this Part`
    `s 681(2)(e) anything done in pursuance of an order of the court under Part 26 or 26A`
    `s 681(2)(f) anything done under an arrangement made in pursuance of section 110 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Article 96 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989`
    `s 681(2)(g) anything done under an arrangement between a company and its creditors that is binding on the creditors by virtue of Part 1 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Part 2 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989`
    `s 681(2) any other transaction`

-- src:8991 | (1) Neither section 678 nor section 679 prohibits a transaction to which this section applies.
-- src:8992 | (2) Those transactions are—
-- src:8993 | (a) a distribution of the company's assets by way of—
-- src:8994 | (i) dividend lawfully made, or
-- src:8995 | (ii) distribution in the course of a company's winding up;
-- src:8996 | (b) an allotment of bonus shares;
-- src:8997 | (c) a reduction of capital under Chapter 10 of Part 17;
-- src:8998 | (d) a redemption of shares under Chapter 3 or a purchase of shares under Chapter 4 of this Part;
-- src:8999 | (e) anything done in pursuance of an order of the court under Part 26 or 26A (order sanctioning compromise or arrangement with members or creditors);
-- src:9000 | (f) anything done under an arrangement made in pursuance of section 110 of the Insolvency Act 1986 (c. 45) or Article 96 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989 (S.I. 1989/2405 (N.I. 19)) (liquidator in winding up accepting shares as consideration for sale of company's property);
-- src:9001 | (g) anything done under an arrangement made between a company and its creditors that is binding on the creditors by virtue of Part 1 of the Insolvency Act 1986 or Part 2 of the Insolvency (Northern Ireland) Order 1989 (S.I. 1989/2405 (N.I. 19)).
@ref s 681 Unconditional exceptions (src:8991-9001)
GIVEN transaction IS A `s 681(2) transaction`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 681(1) neither section 678 nor section 679 prohibits the transaction` MEANS
    CONSIDER transaction
    WHEN `s 681(2) any other transaction` THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "Those transactions are— (a) ... (g)": section 681 applies to the listed transactions (a list closed by "are": marginal reading, fork F-are)
    OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- ---- s 682: conditional exceptions ------------------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:9009 | (a) where the lending of money is part of the ordinary business of the company, the lending of money in the ordinary course of the company's business;
@ref s 682(2)(a) Lending of money in the ordinary course of the company's business (src:9009-9009)
GIVEN `the lending of money is part of the ordinary business of the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transaction is the lending of money in the ordinary course of the company's business` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 682(2)(a) the transaction is a lending of money in the ordinary course` MEANS
    IF `the lending of money is part of the ordinary business of the company` AND `the transaction is the lending of money in the ordinary course of the company's business`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "where the lending of money is part of the ordinary business of the company, the lending of money in the ordinary course of the company's business" (this limb does not apply; another limb may)

-- src:9010 | (b) the provision by the company, in good faith in the interests of the company or its holding company, of financial assistance for the purposes of an employees' share scheme;
@ref s 682(2)(b) Assistance for the purposes of an employees' share scheme provided in good faith (src:9010-9010)
GIVEN `s 1166 the scheme is an employees' share scheme` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the assistance is provided in good faith in the interests of the company or its holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 682(2)(b) the transaction is the provision of assistance for the purposes of an employees' share scheme` MEANS
    IF (NOT `the assistance is provided in good faith in the interests of the company or its holding company`)
    THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "the provision by the company, in good faith in the interests of the company or its holding company, of financial assistance for the purposes of an employees' share scheme" (this limb does not apply; another limb may)
    ELSE CONSIDER `s 1166 the scheme is an employees' share scheme`
         WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "for the purposes of an employees' share scheme" (this limb does not apply; another limb may)
         WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the scheme is an employees' share scheme is s 1166, answered by the caller

-- src:9011 | (c) the provision of financial assistance by the company for the purposes of or in connection with anything done by the company (or another company in the same group) for the purpose of enabling or facilitating transactions in shares in the first-mentioned company or its holding company between, and involving the acquisition of beneficial ownership of those shares by—
-- src:9012 | (i) bona fide employees or former employees of that company (or another company in the same group), or
-- src:9013 | (ii) spouses or civil partners, widows, widowers or surviving civil partners, or minor children or step-children of any such employees or former employees;
@ref s 682(2)(c) Assistance in connection with transactions in shares between, and involving the acquisition of beneficial ownership by, employees and their families (src:9011-9013)
GIVEN `the assistance is for the purposes of or in connection with anything done by the company (or another company in the same group) for the purpose of enabling or facilitating transactions in shares in the company or its holding company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transactions are between, and involve the acquisition of beneficial ownership by, bona fide employees or former employees of that company (or another company in the same group)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the transactions are between, and involve the acquisition of beneficial ownership by, spouses or civil partners, widows, widowers or surviving civil partners, or minor children or step-children of such employees or former employees` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 682(2)(c) the transaction is assistance in connection with transactions in shares by employees or their families` MEANS
    IF `the assistance is for the purposes of or in connection with anything done by the company (or another company in the same group) for the purpose of enabling or facilitating transactions in shares in the company or its holding company`
       AND (`the transactions are between, and involve the acquisition of beneficial ownership by, bona fide employees or former employees of that company (or another company in the same group)`
            OR `the transactions are between, and involve the acquisition of beneficial ownership by, spouses or civil partners, widows, widowers or surviving civil partners, or minor children or step-children of such employees or former employees`)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(c) the provision of financial assistance by the company for the purposes of or in connection with anything done by the company (or another company in the same group) for the purpose of enabling or facilitating transactions in shares ... between, and involving the acquisition of beneficial ownership of those shares by— (i) bona fide employees or former employees ..., or (ii) spouses or civil partners ..." (this limb does not apply; another limb may)

-- src:9014 | (d) the making by the company of loans to persons (other than directors) employed in good faith by the company with a view to enabling those persons to acquire fully paid shares in the company or its holding company to be held by them by way of beneficial ownership.
@ref s 682(2)(d) Loans to persons (other than directors) employed in good faith to enable them to acquire fully paid shares (src:9014-9014)
GIVEN `the loan is made to a person employed in good faith by the company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is a director` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the loan is made with a view to enabling the person to acquire fully paid shares in the company or its holding company to be held by him by way of beneficial ownership` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 682(2)(d) the transaction is a loan to a person other than a director to acquire fully paid shares` MEANS
    -- fork F-other-than: a loan to a director is read as outside limb (d): JUST FALSE for this limb, and another limb may still apply; the other reading answers NOTHING
    IF `the loan is made to a person employed in good faith by the company`
       AND (NOT `the person is a director`)
       AND `the loan is made with a view to enabling the person to acquire fully paid shares in the company or its holding company to be held by him by way of beneficial ownership`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(d) the making by the company of loans to persons (other than directors) employed in good faith by the company with a view to enabling those persons to acquire fully paid shares in the company or its holding company to be held by them by way of beneficial ownership" (this limb does not apply; another limb may)

-- src:9008 | (2) The transactions to which this section applies are—
-- src:9009 | (a) where the lending of money is part of the ordinary business of the company, the lending of money in the ordinary course of the company's business;
-- src:9010 | (b) the provision by the company, in good faith in the interests of the company or its holding company, of financial assistance for the purposes of an employees' share scheme;
-- src:9011 | (c) the provision of financial assistance by the company for the purposes of or in connection with anything done by the company (or another company in the same group) for the purpose of enabling or facilitating transactions in shares in the first-mentioned company or its holding company between, and involving the acquisition of beneficial ownership of those shares by—
-- src:9012 | (i) bona fide employees or former employees of that company (or another company in the same group), or
-- src:9013 | (ii) spouses or civil partners, widows, widowers or surviving civil partners, or minor children or step-children of any such employees or former employees;
-- src:9014 | (d) the making by the company of loans to persons (other than directors) employed in good faith by the company with a view to enabling those persons to acquire fully paid shares in the company or its holding company to be held by them by way of beneficial ownership.
@ref s 682(2) The transactions to which section 682 applies (src:9008-9014)
GIVEN `s 682(2)(a) the transaction is a lending of money in the ordinary course` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 682(2)(b) the transaction is the provision of assistance for the purposes of an employees' share scheme` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 682(2)(c) the transaction is assistance in connection with transactions in shares by employees or their families` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 682(2)(d) the transaction is a loan to a person other than a director to acquire fully paid shares` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 682(2) the transaction is one to which section 682 applies` MEANS
    IF (`s 682(2)(a) the transaction is a lending of money in the ordinary course` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
       OR (`s 682(2)(b) the transaction is the provision of assistance for the purposes of an employees' share scheme` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
       OR (`s 682(2)(c) the transaction is assistance in connection with transactions in shares by employees or their families` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
       OR (`s 682(2)(d) the transaction is a loan to a person other than a director to acquire fully paid shares` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF (`s 682(2)(a) the transaction is a lending of money in the ordinary course` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
            AND (`s 682(2)(b) the transaction is the provision of assistance for the purposes of an employees' share scheme` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
            AND (`s 682(2)(c) the transaction is assistance in connection with transactions in shares by employees or their families` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
            AND (`s 682(2)(d) the transaction is a loan to a person other than a director to acquire fully paid shares` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "The transactions to which this section applies are— (a) ... (b) ... (c) ... (d) ..." (a list closed by "are": marginal reading, fork F-are)
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): a limb is not known

-- src:9003 | (1) Neither section 678 nor section 679 prohibits a transaction to which this section applies—
-- src:9004 | (a) if the company giving the assistance is a private company, or
-- src:9005 | (b) if the company giving the assistance is a public company and—
-- src:9006 | (i) the company has net assets that are not reduced by the giving of the assistance, or
-- src:9007 | (ii) to the extent that those assets are so reduced, the assistance is provided out of distributable profits.
@ref s 682(1) Conditional exceptions: neither section 678 nor 679 prohibits the transaction if the company is private, or is public with net assets not reduced or assistance out of distributable profits (src:9003-9007)
GIVEN `s 682(2) the transaction is one to which section 682 applies` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `the company giving the assistance is a private company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company giving the assistance is a public company` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the company has net assets that are not reduced by the giving of the assistance` IS A BOOLEAN
      `to the extent that those assets are so reduced, the assistance is provided out of distributable profits` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 682(1) neither section 678 nor section 679 prohibits the transaction` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 682(2) the transaction is one to which section 682 applies`
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "prohibits a transaction to which this section applies"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): whether the transaction is within the section is not known
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN
         IF `the company giving the assistance is a private company`
            OR (`the company giving the assistance is a public company`
                AND (`the company has net assets that are not reduced by the giving of the assistance`
                     OR `to the extent that those assets are so reduced, the assistance is provided out of distributable profits`))
         THEN JUST TRUE
         ELSE JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "(a) if the company giving the assistance is a private company, or (b) if the company giving the assistance is a public company and— (i) the company has net assets that are not reduced by the giving of the assistance, or (ii) to the extent that those assets are so reduced, the assistance is provided out of distributable profits"

-- src:9015 | (3) The references in this section to “net assets” are to the amount by which the aggregate of the company's assets exceeds the aggregate of its liabilities.
@ref s 682(3) The references to "net assets" are to the amount by which the aggregate of the company's assets exceeds the aggregate of its liabilities (src:9015-9015)
GIVEN `the aggregate of the company's assets, as stated in the company's accounting records immediately before the financial assistance is given` IS A NUMBER
      `the aggregate of the company's liabilities, as section 682(4) works them out` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 682(3) the net assets of the company` MEANS
    `the aggregate of the company's assets, as stated in the company's accounting records immediately before the financial assistance is given` MINUS `the aggregate of the company's liabilities, as section 682(4) works them out`

-- src:9016 | (4) For this purpose—
-- src:9017 | (a) the amount of both assets and liabilities shall be taken to be as stated in the company's accounting records immediately before the financial assistance is given, and
-- src:9018 | (b) “liabilities” includes any amount retained as reasonably necessary for the purpose of providing for a liability the nature of which is clearly defined and that is either likely to be incurred or certain to be incurred but uncertain as to amount or as to the date on which it will arise.
@ref s 682(4) The amounts are as stated in the accounting records immediately before the assistance is given; liabilities include amounts retained for a liability clearly defined (src:9016-9018)
GIVEN `the liabilities as stated in the company's accounting records immediately before the financial assistance is given` IS A NUMBER
      `the amount retained as reasonably necessary for the purpose of providing for a liability the nature of which is clearly defined and that is either likely to be incurred or certain to be incurred but uncertain as to amount or date` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 682(4) the aggregate of the company's liabilities` MEANS
    `the liabilities as stated in the company's accounting records immediately before the financial assistance is given`
      PLUS `the amount retained as reasonably necessary for the purpose of providing for a liability the nature of which is clearly defined and that is either likely to be incurred or certain to be incurred but uncertain as to amount or date`

-- src:9019 | (5) For the purposes of subsection (2)(c) a company is in the same group as another company if it is a holding company or subsidiary of that company or a subsidiary of a holding company of that company.
@ref s 682(5) A company is in the same group as another if it is a holding company or subsidiary of that company or a subsidiary of a holding company of that company (src:9019-9019)
GIVEN `s 1159(1) the company is a holding company or a subsidiary of that company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 1159(1) the company is a subsidiary of a holding company of that company` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 682(5) the company is in the same group as the other company` MEANS
    IF (`s 1159(1) the company is a holding company or a subsidiary of that company` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
       OR (`s 1159(1) the company is a subsidiary of a holding company of that company` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE IF (`s 1159(1) the company is a holding company or a subsidiary of that company` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
            AND (`s 1159(1) the company is a subsidiary of a holding company of that company` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
         THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "a company is in the same group as another company if it is a holding company or subsidiary of that company or a subsidiary of a holding company of that company"
         ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): holding company and subsidiary are s 1159 (the keel), answered by the caller

-- ---- s 683: definitions for this Chapter -----------------------------------------------------------------

-- src:9022 | (1) In this Chapter—
-- src:9023 | “distributable profits”, in relation to the giving of any financial assistance—
-- src:9024 | (a) means those profits out of which the company could lawfully make a distribution equal in value to that assistance, and
-- src:9025 | (b) includes, in a case where the financial assistance consists of or includes, or is treated as arising in consequence of, the sale, transfer or other disposition of a non-cash asset, any profit that, if the company were to make a distribution of that character would be available for that purpose (see section 846); and
@ref s 683(1) "distributable profits" in relation to the giving of financial assistance (src:9022-9025)
GIVEN `s 830 the profits available for distribution` IS A NUMBER
      `the assistance consists of or includes, or is treated as arising in consequence of, the sale, transfer or other disposition of a non-cash asset` IS A BOOLEAN
      `s 846 the profit that would be available for a distribution of that character` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 683(1) the distributable profits in relation to the giving of the financial assistance` MEANS
    `s 830 the profits available for distribution`
      PLUS (IF `the assistance consists of or includes, or is treated as arising in consequence of, the sale, transfer or other disposition of a non-cash asset`
            THEN `s 846 the profit that would be available for a distribution of that character`
            ELSE 0)

@ref s 683(1) "distributable profits" in relation to the giving of financial assistance (src:9022-9025)
GIVEN `the value of the financial assistance` IS A NUMBER
      `the distributable profits in relation to the giving of the assistance` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 683(1)(a) the assistance is covered by the distributable profits` MEANS
    `the value of the financial assistance` AT MOST `the distributable profits in relation to the giving of the assistance`

-- src:9026 | “distribution” has the same meaning as in Part 23 (distributions) (see section 829).
@ref s 683(1) "distribution" has the same meaning as in Part 23 (src:9026-9026)
GIVEN `s 829 the payment is a distribution` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 683(1) the payment is a distribution for the purposes of Chapter 2` MEANS
    CONSIDER `s 829 the payment is a distribution`
    WHEN JUST TRUE THEN JUST TRUE
    WHEN JUST FALSE THEN JUST FALSE -- FALSE-kind (the borrowed definition says no, supplied as an input): "“distribution” has the same meaning as in Part 23 (distributions) (see section 829)"
    WHEN NOTHING THEN NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (points outside the text): the meaning is Part 23 (coa18)

-- src:9028 | (a) a reference to a person incurring a liability includes his changing his financial position by making an agreement or arrangement (whether enforceable or unenforceable, and whether made on his own account or with any other person) or by any other means, and
@ref s 683(2)(a) A reference to a person incurring a liability includes his changing his financial position by an agreement or arrangement or by any other means (src:9028-9028)
GIVEN `he changes his financial position by making an agreement or arrangement (whether enforceable or unenforceable, and whether made on his own account or with any other person)` IS A BOOLEAN
      `he changes his financial position by any other means` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 683(2)(a) the person incurs a liability` MEANS
    IF `he changes his financial position by making an agreement or arrangement (whether enforceable or unenforceable, and whether made on his own account or with any other person)` OR `he changes his financial position by any other means`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "a reference to a person incurring a liability includes his changing his financial position"

-- src:9029 | (b) a reference to a company giving financial assistance for the purposes of reducing or discharging a liability incurred by a person for the purpose of the acquisition of shares includes its giving such assistance for the purpose of wholly or partly restoring his financial position to what it was before the acquisition took place.
@ref s 683(2)(b) A reference to giving assistance for the purposes of reducing or discharging a liability includes giving it to restore his financial position (src:9029-9029)
GIVEN `the assistance is given for the purpose of reducing or discharging a liability incurred by a person for the purpose of the acquisition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the assistance is given for the purpose of wholly or partly restoring his financial position to what it was before the acquisition took place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 683(2)(b) the assistance is given for the purposes of reducing or discharging the liability` MEANS
    IF `the assistance is given for the purpose of reducing or discharging a liability incurred by a person for the purpose of the acquisition` OR `the assistance is given for the purpose of wholly or partly restoring his financial position to what it was before the acquisition took place`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING -- NOTHING-kind (includes): "includes its giving such assistance for the purpose of wholly or partly restoring his financial position to what it was before the acquisition took place"
